Subject: Feasibility Study & ROI - ASR Smart Tiering Deployment (Replication Cost Optimization)

Hi [Manager's Name],

Following the technical validation of our Azure Site Recovery (ASR) "Smart Tiering" architecture, I have finalized the financial and technical impact study on our production environments.

Using our metric extraction script across all subscriptions, we mapped the write speeds (MB/s) of all protected VMs. To guarantee absolute operational safety and avoid any risks to our RPO/RTO SLAs, I based the analysis on maximum write peaks rather than smoothed averages.

Since the technical limit for ASR on Standard HDD storage is 8 MB/s per VM, we have formally excluded applications exceeding this threshold (e.g., OMEGA, EVEREST, LOG MGMT, SAPP4SCOMPUTE, etc.).

Here is the breakdown of the analysis:

Secured Scope (Excluded from Smart Tiering): 327,641 GiB (31% of our total volume). These disks will remain on Premium SSD to safely absorb their peak write loads without risking replication desynchronization.

Eligible Scope (Smart Tiering Candidates): 721,936 GiB. These disks operate well below the critical 8 MB/s threshold and are currently running on dormant Premium SSDs.

Financial Impact (ROI):

The current cost of this eligible scope on Premium SSD is approximately €90,200 / month.

By downgrading these passive replicas to Standard HDD via our automation, the cost will drop to approximately €30,300 / month.

This optimization represents a net saving of ~€60,000 per month (over €700,000 per year), translating to a 66% reduction in storage costs for this scope.

The Failover and Failback Runbooks, along with the Standard Operating Procedure (SOP), are now finalized. They are secured with strict filters to ensure there is zero impact on active VMs.

